    "id": "q08",
    "topic": "particle-to",
    "question": "How is the particle と (to) used to list nouns? What is its role when used before を?",
    "answer": "The particle **と** connects nouns into a complete list, meaning \"and.\" When used before **を**, **を** marks the entire list as the direct object.  \nJapanese (romaji) — translation  \nラーメンとぎょうざを食べます (ra-men to gyouza wo tabemasu) — I eat ramen and gyoza.  \nねこといぬをみます (neko to inu wo mimasu) — I see a cat and a dog.  \n**と** creates a specific list, and **を** treats the whole group as one object.",
