    "question": "How do you form the te-form of かく (kaku)? What is the general pattern for く verbs?",
    "answer": "The te-form of かく (kaku) is かいて (kaite). Most く verbs follow a general pattern where the final く changes to いて in the te-form. However, there are important exceptions: いく (iku) becomes いって (itte), and くる (kuru) becomes きて (kite).  \nJapanese (romaji) — translation  \nかいてみます (kaite mimasu) — I will try writing.  \nいってきます (itte kimasu) — I will go and come back.  \nThe te-form for most く verbs is ～いて, but いく and くる are irregular.",
