    "answer": "おきる (okiru) is a Group 2 verb (ru-verb) because it ends with **る**. Group 2 verbs are called **ru-verbs** and always end in **る** in their dictionary form. Examples include **たべる** (taberu, to eat) and **みる** (miru, to see).  \nEven though some Group 1 verbs (u-verbs) like **かえる** (kaeru, to return) also end with **る**, they are classified as Group 1 because their dictionary form ends with **える** (a u-verb ending).  \n**Summary**: おきる is a Group 2 verb because it ends with **る**, not **える**.",
