    "question": "Translate: 'I drink coffee and tea.'",
    "answer": "Japanese (romaji) — I drink coffee and tea.  \n私はコーヒーとお茶を飲みます。  \n- **コーヒー (koohii)** = coffee  \n- **お茶 (ocha)** = tea  \n- **を (wo)** marks the entire list (coffee and tea) as the direct object.  \n- **と (to)** connects the two nouns into a list.  \n- **飲みます (nomimasu)** = drink (polite form).  \nThis follows the rule: **object comes before the verb**, and **を marks the whole list as the direct object**.",
